00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,910
I just can't find...

266
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,910
Top drawer.

267
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:35,200
Why? you need one too?

268
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:37,790
Oh, yeah.

269
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:40,330
Found them!

270
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:45,250
There's only one.

271
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:48,210
Monica!

272
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:52,470
Uh, we'll be right there. We're just trying to decide something.

273
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,390
Rachel?

274
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:09,900
Hey.

275
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:13,950
They're trying to decide something.

276
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:13,950
Good. Good, good.

277
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:24,460
So is, um... So was your mustache... Did it used to be different?

278
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:28,710
No.

279
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:34,590
How do you, uh, you know, keep it so neat?

280
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,680
I Have A little comb.

281
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:44,060
What do you call that?

282
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:44,060
A mustache comb.

283
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:45,650
Thank you.

284
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:50,860
Okay, I will do your laundry for one month.

285
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,240
No!

286
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,240
Okay, okay!

287
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,070
I will, I will, I will...

288
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:57,950
I will clean the apartment for two months.

289
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:02,460
I'll give this to you now, if you tell me where we keep the dustpan.

290
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:13,840
So were you in Nam?

291
00:16:18,470 --> 00:16:20,680
Rock, paper, scissors?

292
00:16:18,470 --> 00:16:20,680
Gotcha.

293
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:23,020
One, two, three.

294
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:24,850
Yes!

295
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:28,310
Fine. Go have sex.

296
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:33,150
No! You have got it completely wrong!

297
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:36,200
John Savage was Deer Hunter, no legs.

298
00:16:36,450 --> 00:16:39,330
Jon Voight was Coming Home, couldn't feel his legs.

299
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:43,710
No, you've got it totally the other way around, my friend. Jon Voight...

300
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:45,710
Honey? Ahem.

301
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:45,710
What? Oh.

302
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,800
Shall we?

303
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,800
It's not gonna happen.

304
00:16:57,050 --> 00:17:00,300
They're doing it tonight. We can do it tomorrow.

305
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:06,560
Uh, in the future, if I could see the schedule beforehand...

306
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,150
So when I woke up this morning...

307
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:15,530
he'd stolen all the insoles out of my shoes!

308
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:16,820
Why?

309
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:20,870
He thinks I slept with his ex-girlfriend and killed his fish.

310
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,910
Why would you kill his fish?

311
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:29,000
Because sometimes after you sleep with someone...

312
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:31,590
you have to kill a fish.

313
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:35,130
Chandler, honey...

314
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:36,510
I'm sorry.

315
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:39,050
Can we watch Joey's show now, please?

316
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:41,100
Wait. He's not here yet.

317
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:43,600
He's on the show, he knows what happens.

318
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:47,230
I'm fine about my problem now, by the way.

319
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,690
Amber...

320
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:54,730
I want you to know I'll always be there for you...

321
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:56,990
as a friend and as your brother.

322
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,240
Oh, Drake.

323
00:17:59,950 --> 00:18:01,240
Hard day, huh?

324
00:18:01,490 --> 00:18:04,160
First the medical award, now this?

325
00:18:04,330 --> 00:18:07,660
Some guys are just lucky, I guess. Ha, ha.

326
00:18:07,830 --> 00:18:09,500
Dr. Ramoray...

327
00:18:09,670 --> 00:18:12,380
report to First floor Emergency stat.

328
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,880
Well, then...

329
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:17,380
I, uh, guess that's me.

330
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:23,220
Anyone else need to go on the elevator? Dr. Horton? Dr. Wong?

331
00:18:23,390 --> 00:18:26,470
No, no. They only said you.

332
00:18:28,730 --> 00:18:31,230
Oh, okay. All right.

333
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,070
I love you, Drake.

334
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,070
Yeah, whatever.

335
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:38,070
Oh, no!

336
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:38,070
Drake, look out!

337
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:45,030
Did they just kill off Joey?

338
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:45,030
No!

339
00:18:47,450 --> 00:18:49,160
Now maybe.

340
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:53,750
Come on! Open up! We want to talk to you!

341
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,420
I don't feel like talking!

342
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:57,420
Come on! We care about you.

343
00:18:57,590 --> 00:19:01,880
We're worried about you.

344
00:18:57,590 --> 00:19:01,880
And some of us have to pee!

345
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:07,560
I'm sorry, Joey.

346
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:13,150
Listen, sorry about your death. That really sucks.

347
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:17,150
We came over as soon as We saw.

348
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:17,150
How could you not tell us?

349
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:21,110
I don't know. I was kind of hoping no one would ever find out.

350
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:25,320
Well, maybe they could find a way to bring you back.

351
00:19:25,490 --> 00:19:31,000
No, they said that when they found my body, my brain was so smashed in...

352
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:34,830
that the only doctor who could've saved me was me.

353
00:19:36,590 --> 00:19:38,880
It's supposed to be some kind of irony.

354
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,550
But Joey, you're gonna be fine.

355
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:46,180
You don't need that show. It was just a dumb soap opera.

356
00:19:46,390 --> 00:19:49,560
This was the greatest thing that ever happened to me.

357
00:19:49,770 --> 00:19:52,390
Yes! I was going to incorporate that.

358
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:56,980
Oh, good, here's Monica. She'll have something nice to say.

359
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:02,070
Um, I straightened out your shower curtain so you won't get mildew.

360
00:20:03,450 --> 00:20:05,110
What? To me, that's nice.

361
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,490
It's gonna be okay. You know that.

362
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,750
No, I don't.

363
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:15,330
It's like you work your whole life for something...

364
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,710
and you think that when you get it...

365
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,300
it'll never be as good as you thought.

366
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:22,260
But this so was.

367
00:20:22,630 --> 00:20:24,220
It changed everything.

368
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:27,640
Like, the other day, I got this credit card application...

369
00:20:27,890 --> 00:20:30,180
and I was pre-approved!

370
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:36,100
Huh? I've never been pre-approved for anything in my life!

371
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,860
I'm sorry, man.

372
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:41,360
I don't know if this'll mean anything to you...

373
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:44,200
but you'll always be pre-approved with us.

374
00:20:45,490 --> 00:20:47,160
No, that means nothing to me.

375
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,000
Ahh!

376
00:20:54,370 --> 00:20:56,250
Pecan sandy? Just made them.

377
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:59,290
Yeah, all right.

378
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,590
Are these raisins?

379
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:04,220
Uh, sure, why not?

380
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,810
Listen, Eddie. Um, ahem.

381
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:17,850
I've been thinking about our living situation and, uh...

382
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:19,190
Why are you smiling?

383
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:22,780
I got a little surprise. Look. There's a new fishy.

384
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:24,860
I named him, uh...

385
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:27,610
Chandler, you know, after you.

386
00:21:36,790 --> 00:21:39,540
Well, that's not even a real fish.

387
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:43,300
No, that's a Goldfish cracker.

388
00:21:45,170 --> 00:21:46,840
So, what's your point, man?

389
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,890
Okay, good night.

390
00:21:53,810 --> 00:21:56,230
You big freak of nature.

391
00:22:12,330 --> 00:22:14,200
Aah.

392
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:19,670
Hey.

393
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:25,210
Whoo. Brisk tonight.

394
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:25,210
Oh, man.

395
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:28,760
Let's never speak of this.

396
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:28,760
You got it.

